        "marketStrings": [
          {
            "key": "closedCaptioning",
            "value": "The personal closed captioning device displays feature film dialogue and other audio in the form of English-language text for individuals who are deaf or hard of hearing."
          },
          {
            "key": "descriptiveAudio",
            "value": "The descriptive audio headset provides individuals who are blind or have low vision with an English-language narration of the details of the feature presentation that can't be understood by the soundtrack alone."
          },
          {
            "key": "assistedListening",
            "value": "Upon request at the box office, we provide assistive listening headsets with amplified audio for those individuals who are hard of hearing. For guests who prefer to use their own hearing aids, neck loops, or cochlear implants, our assistive listening headsets have a 3.5mm headphone jack to connect to those devices."
          },
          {
            "key": "latePolicy",
            "value": "In order to ensure the highest quality experience for all guests, you may not enter a movie after it has started. We’d love to see you up to 30 minutes early. Running late? No worries, we will happily exchange your ticket for a different showtime or a raincheck to a future show."
          }
        ]
      }
